  <div class="content-callout">
    <h2>The Short Answer</h2>
    <p>
      Pick <strong>Saily</strong> if you want a VPN and ad-blocker bundled into the same eSIM and don't want to reinstall a new profile at every border on a multi-country trip. Pick <strong>SimLocal</strong> if you want a real bundled phone number on a UK trip, a no-questions refund policy, or the option to walk up to a staffed airport counter instead of sorting it out yourself. Both sit in the same "Cheap" price bracket on this site and both sell fixed-GB plans rather than true unlimited data, so the real decision is about which extras you actually need, not which is cheaper on paper.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>The Core Difference: Security Bundle vs. Local Number Bundle</h2>
  <p>
    Saily is NordVPN's own eSIM spin-off (built by Nord Security itself, not a partner deal), so every plan ships with ad blocking, malware/phishing site blocking, and a virtual-location tool included. It also sells one universal eSIM that keeps working as you cross into a new supported country, so you're not swapping profiles at each border.
  </p>
  <p>
    SimLocal's edge is different: most of its UK plans come bundled with a real UK phone number for calls and texts, not just data, something Saily doesn't offer at all. SimLocal backs that with a "No Quibble Refunds" policy (cancel for any reason, no explanation needed) and, unusually for an eSIM-only seller, a staffed counter at Heathrow if you'd rather have someone walk you through setup in person.
  </p>

